The declared_user field represents the supplied participants with role=user, whose canonical identity is already declared. Those participant IDs are accounted for by that field and are unavailable to subjects. Put only claims that describe the user in declared_user.supporting_claims; use an empty list when the user only reports other people's facts. Describe other people and things in subjects, including people mentioned by the user. Do not create another subject for the declared user. Authorship alone does not make a claim about its speaker.
